@@ -59,3 +59,29 @@ This template uses the following placeholders:
 - `backend/nakama/.env.cloudrun.generated` (GitHub environment variable scaffold for Cloud Run workflow inputs)
 - `backend/nakama/.env.local.generated` (local runtime defaults)
 - `backend/nakama/.env.render.generated` (Render fallback env scaffold)
+
+## Authenticated platform identity exchange
+
+The template RPC and internal exchange helper require authenticated nonblank
+`ctx.userId`; client payloads cannot select the user, game or exchange credential.
+The server uses `GAME_ID` and a dedicated `TPX_NAKAMA_EXCHANGE_KEY` matching that
+game/environment's gateway mapping. Only identity requests receive
+`x-nakama-exchange-key`. Missing/invalid configuration fails before HTTP. Use at
+least 32 URL-safe characters for an approved server credential; no value is
+provided and no provisioning is performed. Never use PLATFORM_INTERNAL_KEY as a
+fallback or export this value in Godot/client configuration.
+
+Render's blueprint declares a server-only unsynced setting, and start.sh forwards
+it into Nakama runtime.env. Cloud Run requires a separately approved secret-backed
+environment reference. Local Compose mounts local.yml directly; use a private
+runtime-config override and avoid its traced (-ecx) command for secrets. Generated
+onboarding env files do not provision this key; inject it through approved secret
+management, not source manifests. Existing generated repos do not inherit these
+changes automatically. See docs/IDENTITY_EXCHANGE_ROLLOUT.md in the canonical repo.
+
+No new template tokens are introduced; bootstrap-game.ps1 retains token ownership.
+The NakamaService/ShopModal/ThemeManager sibling interfaces were inspected and
+require no identity RPC/client contract change. PowerShell is unavailable on this
+Mac, so the normal audit_repo.ps1, bootstrap-game.ps1 and verify_repo.ps1 workflows
+were not run. Node tests perform limited token-substitution/runtime selection
+checks, not a claim that full Godot/bootstrap verification passed.
