+# Identity exchange rollout inventory
+
+Inspected with verified TeraPixelGames access on 2026-10-20. Source-only inventory;
+actual deployed runtimes/exposure are unverified. GitHub indexed searches returned
+68 literal-route matches and 19 configuration-name matches, each with
+incomplete_results=false. Searches can omit unindexed/dynamic callers; this is not
+proof of exhaustive deployed coverage. The active LumaRush module was also read
+locally. No credentials or production identities were used.
+
+## Canonical fixes prepared locally
+
+- ArcadeCore backend/templates/nakama-game-backend/nakama/modules/index.js:
+  both RPC and internal helper now require ctx.userId and dedicated server proof.
+  Runtime entrypoint is index.js; copied consumer modules have the same old blob.
+- ArcadeCore backend/server.js: legacy guest/email proxy disabled with 503;
+  never grant it an exchange key without a genuine authenticated identity design.
+- terapixel-platform templates/nakama-game-backend/nakama/modules/index.js:
+  separate local compatibility-scaffold patch fixes Nakama callback registration,
+  payload-selected IDs and missing game-scoped credential proof. Use canonical
+  ArcadeCore for new scaffolds. This platform patch remains unpublished.
+- LumaRush backend/nakama/modules/lumarush.js is the configured active entrypoint;
+  index.js is an alternative template-derived path. Both are covered by draft
+  https://github.com/Terapixel-Games/LumaRush/pull/13.
+
+## Identical vulnerable generated modules on default branches
+
+All 21 game modules below share the exact Git blob
+4b5209bf5b04e2a25d399fc6ae9f9eba621570d0 with the old canonical template. They prefer
+payload nakama_user_id over ctx.userId and exchange without backend proof.
+The feature-branch fixes are not reflected in these default-branch snapshots.
+
